{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794230245,"nonce":"19VHIwzO/NQq99vyDsELgJQ7QSI=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-493a53c-integration` (4de5fc8..0bed642).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/ui/tooltip.rs: new custom Widget `tip(content, label)` with `.shortcut()` and `.enabled()`. Overlay with 350ms cold delay and a warm group (instant open within 300ms of another tooltip). Fade 120ms in and 80ms out via `Animation`, with a 4px slide. Pure `place()` prefers below, flips above, shifts horizontally, 8px gap. Closes on press, scroll and cursor leave. Redraws only while pending or animating. 11 unit tests.\n- src/theme/style.rs: `tooltip(alpha)` container style (surface, border, soft shadow, radius::MD).\n- src/ui/components.rs: `icon_pill` now takes a label; new `icon_square_button` (tooltip, optional press).\n- src/ui/screen.rs: tooltips on all 5 top-bar icon buttons (theme label shows the current mode), the collapsed sidebar nav items (enabled only when collapsed), the epic chevron, the row close/reopen toggle and the root remove button.\n- src/ui/detail.rs: close button uses `icon_square_button` (\"Close details\").\n- src/ui/done.rs: close button uses `icon_square_button` (\"Close\").\n- src/ui/mod.rs: registers the `tooltip` module.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 1 findings — 1 auto, 0 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- Warm-group state is a thread_local `LAST_SHOWN` timestamp, not app state. A pending tooltip re-reads warmth each event, so the instant open also works when moving to an earlier widget in the tree (the scan's finding, fixed).\n- The tooltip body is rebuilt inside `overlay()` on each frame with the current alpha. iced re-runs overlay layout on every draw, and this gives the fade and the slide without renderer opacity support.\n- Shortcut hints are supported but no call site sets one; L5 fills them in.\n- Sidebar tooltips are enabled only while the sidebar target state is collapsed, because expanded items already show labels.\n- The animation, fade and overlay behaviour is not exercised by tests, and the app was not run visually. Only the placement function and the open-delay state machine are unit-tested.","files":null}]}